        <body>
            <div xml:id="d240">

                <pb facs="0431" n="369" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg369"/>

                <head>No. 235.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Read to Mr. Evarts</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Athens</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-03-13"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 13, 1878</date>.
                        (Received April 13.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 370.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: To-day the King lunched on board the
                    Vandalia with General Grant, and spent two hours in conversation.</p>
                <p>The King came officially, in uniform. He has indeed seized every occasion to
                    manifest his respect for General Grant, and the feelings of His Majesty have
                    been fully shared by his subjects, who have displayed, great enthusiasm whenever
                    General Grant has appeared in the streets.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN MEREDITH READ.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
